## CH 11 — "Optimal Sleep." Nishi-Azabu, 9:40 p.m. Minako POV

- **Setting:** eight-seat basement restaurant, four tables, hinoki bar the chef built himself, browned butter and burnt rosemary. Minako in matte black bias-cut silk, one strap, back open to the dimple above her ass, ¥400,000, black lace thong, red bow still in (three phones in the room that might belong to a weekly).
- **RYŌ SAKAGUCHI, established properly.** 26, talent division, charcoal, the jaw people pay for. Five months — her record. He brings a **three-tab color-coded spreadsheet of her career** built at his desk after hours: Hasegawa at 62% recall ("you're not a face he *hired*, you're a face he *uses*"), Ozaki as the blocker (path in via Sugimoto assistant), Fuji's 10 o'clock hospital drama, 11% of sub-three-line parts go to models with no credit. Third tab is portfolio-refresh cost.
- **He is not a villain and the chapter refuses to make him one.** Never late. Never lied. Remembers she hates coriander. Drove to Saitama in the rain in March because she texted one sad word, brought soup and a phone charger. *"a man who thinks about phone chargers."*
- **Minako's thesis line:** *"Men who made her feel like a lit match burned everything, including her, and men who kept her safe kept her in a cell with very good ventilation."* Backstory: **Kaito**, two boyfriends ago — 3 a.m. drive past Chiba, broken heater, bare feet on the dash, ran the tank dry, sunrise on the hood — and was saying *come look at the water* to somebody in Yokohama.
- **Ryō steps out for a two-minute Nakamura call.** Minako's public face drops in the bar mirror — *"mouth slack, eyes flat, the expression that lived under all the others."*
- **She texts Byl.** Contact saved with no surname: **BYL — REPAIRMAN**, typed under the gas station canopy 11 days earlier, untouched since. Cover story to herself: *"Medical due diligence. I'd text a teammate."* She has never texted a teammate.
- **The thread (9:51–9:58).** Scalp check → butterflies came off on a duct → "the duct and a dog with no legal standing" → "I looked at it for free" / "you looked at it with tweezers and a lot of opinions." He's in a Yoyogi stairwell holding a bucket under a dead water heater; Lucy asleep on his jacket on the only dry square meter. She ends up **chin in her hand like a teenager** in the good light. Phone goes face-down the instant she hears footsteps.
- **The ask, and the refusal.** She proposes ice cream in Azabu-Jūban, black sesame, open till one, twenty-minute walk. Ryō: **eleven-twenty**, 6:40 alarm, five full cycles, the fifth is where consolidation happens, Kuroda notices at four. *"Saturday. I'll put it in."* She deploys The Face; he declines it kindly — *"that face, at dinner, in a place like this. Somebody in here is going to have a camera."*
- **She eats most of his sorbet.** He pushes it aside for the sugar.
- **Street level:** his hand on her bare back going up the stairs (she likes it), then the scheduled offer — *"eleven-oh-five, if we go to yours we've got twenty minutes."* **"I've got a headache."** / **"You've had a lot of headaches."** He takes the second taxi because the first driver was smoking.
- **Close:** she counts to ten on the wet street, then texts — *"I'm bored... You're going to come meet me and be interesting at me for an hour. That's the price of the butterflies. Bring the dog."* Byl: *"I'm covered in ceiling."* / *"Perfect. Wear it."* Names the **Sanwa building, Yoyogi** (ugly brown one by the pachinko place) — she shot a tights campaign on that roof in July, **stairwell latch has never caught**, manager complained on camera twice and was ignored. Texts Ryō ***Home safe, sleep well*** from a taxi going the wrong direction, bare feet out of the heels, grinning at the black glass with her teeth showing.

## CH 12 — "Don't Leave, Please." Sanwa roof, 11:31 p.m. Minako POV

- **Roof:** tar and gravel, two condensers out of sync, antenna mast with rust bleeding orange down the guys. Day's heat coming back up through the concrete into the backs of her thighs; cool wet park air off the other side; the two meeting at her ribs.
- **The set, built deliberately.** Heels off by the door (one tipped over) so he'd know she was comfortable; bow out of her hair and wound in her fist so he'd know she was off duty; dress ridden up and left that way. Every line of her arranged to say *I didn't hear you come in.* Her stated purpose: **"You've had a bucket in your hands since nine. So I built you a nice thing to walk into."**
- **Byl arrives in ceiling.** Chalk handprints across the chest, one clean one smeared, gray line of plaster in his eyebrow, wet boots printing on dry tar. Tool bag left downstairs.
- **He looks at her face FIRST** — eyes to eyes, a beat too long to be manners, asking plainly — and only then takes her in, the way he read the violin on Michiru's roof. Sits **closer than a polite man would**, hip a hand's width from her knee.
- **"So. You're in a napkin."** / "It's Aoyama." / "It's a napkin from Aoyama." / "Four hundred thousand yen." / *"For that money you'd think they'd finish it."*
- **He dismantles the set in four seconds** — heels, bow, the whole apparatus — and then does the thing she has no counter for: **"I liked it."** Followed by, unprompted: *"you're the best-looking thing I've seen with my own eyes, and I'm counting the one on the roof with the violin."* / "There was one with a violin?" / **"There's always one with a violin."**
- **She watches the tiredness come off him** — shoulders drop a centimeter and roll back, the face goes quiet, he laughs twice, the second time **head down with his hand over his mouth like a man caught.** She notes it's costing him something to let himself.
- **Her confession, unprompted:** she has a boyfriend, five months, her record, and she inventories his virtues honestly and at length. *"He's a perfect boyfriend... and he's at home right now asleep because sleep is at eleven-twenty. And I'm sitting on a ledge in Yoyogi with my dress around my hips at midnight talking to a man I met in an alley."*
- **Byl immediately moves to leave.** *"Then I should go."*
- **THE GRAB.** Her hand comes off the dog and catches his wrist — Senshi-fast, and she feels his pulse "stop being a thing that circulated and start being a thing she had trapped." **230 lbs of man lifted three inches off the stone and set back down like a bag of rice.** She says **"Don't leave. Please."** Lucy whines — **high, thin, two notes.**
- **MEMORY (triggered by her own voice + the dog's whine).** Silver Millennium. **She is fourteen.** White parapet carved with running moonflowers, warm stone, jasmine off the water gardens. Lower city lying down and glittering — lamps in the terraces, down the switchback, across the bridge over the dry canal — out to where the wall ends and the dust sea goes silver and dead. **Earth overhead**, three-quarters lit, a long white comma of storm turning over an ocean; she found that storm again the next night and the next because it kept turning.
  - Body details: two inches of new height nothing else has caught up to, orange sash tied wrong out of spite, sandals kicked off at the column base, **the long citrine-headed hairpin held point-out — a thing you hold on your way somewhere to use.**
  - Below at the lower gate: **a column forming up, kit bags going up a ramp, a ship's lamps lit. Leaving at dawn.** She's been up there two hours because from there you can see the gate.
  - **Lucille against her hip** — not a dog like her, *exactly* her. One ear turned inside out from running. Plain warm amber eyes.
  - **The dog whines, high, thin, two notes** — and fourteen-year-old Minako turns her head to her left and says out loud: **"Don't leave. Please."** The same words, in the same order, in the same voice.
  - **And there is no one there.** A girl alone on a wall at midnight talking to the air with somebody's dog.
- **THE REDACTION, Minako's version — structurally distinct from Rei's.** Rei went hunting and found clean-edged holes. **Minako gets ambushed and finds the hole *finished*.** She quarters the memory the way she'd quarter a dark street: the space to her left is **not dark, not blurred, does not slide away.** Stone where stone should be, lamplight at the correct angle, moonflower carving running unbroken through it. It is **exactly the width of a big man standing at a parapet with his forearms on the coping**, and it is **the only place in the entire memory she cannot smell anything.** *"Like a photograph somebody cut a figure out of with a scalpel and then handed to a retoucher good enough to paint the background back in."*
  - **The errand survives the reason.** Pin still point-out, she was on her way to the fourth column of the east colonnade, she can feel the itch of the task in her wrist and there is nothing behind it. ← **This is the tally Rei saw scratched in Ch. 10 and found smooth in the present day.**
  - **The name "Lucille" surfaces** — never heard in this life, known like her own measurements.
  - **Artemis has hated dogs for a thousand years and has never once been able to say why.** (Planted. Unexploded.)
  - Her conclusion: *"Somebody had been in her head. The work was old and the work was very, very good."*
- **Coming back:** her grip has left **four white marks pressed into his forearm**, filling slowly to red. He looks at them, looks at her face, **doesn't ask, doesn't rub his arm, doesn't move away.** *"You have got a few things to sort out."*
- **Her terms:** can't do any of it tonight, can't do it here, definitely can't do it out loud — *"But that doesn't mean I can't pretend... for the length of a roof... Stay. Please. Just a little longer, while I figure out what I actually want. That's all I'm asking for and I know exactly how unfair it is."*
- **He has the jaw of a man about to do the correct thing and leave. Lucy whines. He sits back down** — closer than before — takes her hand palm-up in both of his and works the torn muscle below her thumb out of her with real care. The dog lies across both their feet.
- **Close — Byl's one question:** can she tell the perfect man asleep right now the truth? The roof, the thing that just happened to her, the part she isn't saying — say it tomorrow and have him still be there after. *"Because if you can't — if the answer's no — is that what you want the rest of your life to look like?"* (Something in his face she hadn't seen: **young, badly hidden, hungry.**) **They stay until ~2 a.m. She does not answer.**
- **Craft note:** this chapter deliberately breaks the "never end on a question" rule — the break is the chapter's held breath.

## CH 13 — "Controlled Conditions." ENEOS on Hakusan-dōri, Bunkyō, 12:19 a.m. Ami POV. Two nights after the roof

- **Ami's apartment, 11:52 p.m.:** six mats and a hotplate with ambitions, **¥41,000/month in Bunkyō**, taken deliberately over her mother's guest room with its own bath — *"a person who intended to spend her life telling strangers to do hard things ought to know what the hard things cost."* Rice and cheap bagged sprouts nine days running. Rent, utilities, transport, food — **food is the one with the give in it.**
- **The trigger is silence.** The rooftop unit she and Byl rebuilt now runs with no tick at all, and she can't stop hearing the absence. Technical thought → the 2003 phantom defrost routine → the unknown maintainer → **his forearm braced across the housing, corded, not shaking, the badly-closed wrist-to-elbow scar.** She recalls checking **four times** in Ch. 4 whether he'd look at her in the soaked shirt. He never did.
- **Academic state:** semester finished. 20 courses/3 formats, 4 tested out of (22 counting August). Med school entrance **April**; two recommendation letters in hand, third promised. She built slack into the schedule for a load that never came, and **the slack arrived all at once tonight.** Her hands want a task.
- **THE DUTTON & ARON REVERSAL — the spine of the chapter.** In Ch. 4 she filed her attraction as misattribution of arousal (suspension-bridge study) and it held six weeks. Tonight: **23°C, resting pulse 61, no height, no danger, no deadline, no man in the room** — every variable Dutton & Aron ever manipulated sitting at baseline — **and the effect reproduces anyway**, off nothing but the memory of a forearm. Her actual gift named: not speed, but that **she does not flinch from a result that contradicts the model.** *"The result was in."* She gets her wallet.
- **The gas station:** four pumps, canopy light making thirty meters of daytime and stopping dead; moths; ice cabinet compressor cycling every four minutes. Fryer oil vs. eleven-o'clock ammonia vs. the gasoline ghost in the walls.
- **Ami's state of dress:** oversized gray university sweatshirt to the tops of her thighs, sleep shorts, plastic sandals, bob flat on one side from the tatami, **no bra, no makeup, ¥1,100 she has decided she's allowed to spend.**
- **THE NAMES.** Both of them lock up — *"Oh." / "Ah." / "Hi." / "Hello."* — until he clears his throat with real violence and says **"Byl."** She gives **"Ami Mizuno,"** then thanks him for going first because she's **felt badly for six weeks** about never asking. **He laughs until he folds over the hot case: he never got hers either.** Walked down nine flights and hit the street before working out he didn't know what to call her. **Both carried the identical shame for the identical six weeks.** This is what unlocks her.
- **Chit-chat.** He takes *nineteen* + *med school* seriously, which almost nobody does — *"That's not studying. That's a campaign."* His two classes: metallurgy because it pays, linguistics because the room had air conditioning and it became the best thing in his week, ~40 credits toward nothing.
- **The shrine, referenced to her:** roof, gutters, wiring, termite stringer, **18 items and growing, six weeks if nothing underneath is rotten.** *"First time in three years I've known where I'm working on a Thursday."* She files the carefulness in his voice around good news.
- **She asks how his night has been. Direct.** He hesitates a beat and a half at the instant-noodle shelf and says: **"I don't understand girls at all."** Filed deep, corner turned down.
- **THE LAUGH.** She asks if he has a girlfriend and **he laughs** — no deflection, no performance, the unbothered laugh of a man who's been told a small good joke — **and glances over to share it.** Her face does nothing. His smile comes apart. **"No. Sorry. No, I don't."** → over five years, five and a half; record was three months and she spent most of the third deciding; a practiced old both-shoulders shrug. *"So it's not really a live question."*
- Ami's catch: **"You said 'girls.' Plural. Just now. But you meant one."** He concedes it.
- **She pays.** Reaches past his forearm and pushes his chicken and coffee into her pile, card on the reader before his hand gets there. **¥410** — real money to her. *"You can object as much as you'd like. The objection has no mechanism."* Then walks out without checking whether he follows (**the most reckless thing she's done in years**) and feels his shadow come over her before she's three steps across the lot.
- **Outside:** two plastic tables by the ice cabinet at the edge of the light. **Lucy comes off the ground and shoves her skull into Ami's hip hard enough to move her half a step;** Ami goes down on her heels on wet asphalt in sleep shorts, both hands in the ruff, all calculation abandoned.
- **He lays out Minako** (unnamed to Ami — "model," the alley, five men, she waded in without being asked and took two apart, "which is its own thing I haven't sorted out"). The roof: he came off a bucket covered in ceiling and stayed till two. *"It's a change of pace. It's nice."* — **"Same as this."** Then: the roof was flirting for ninety minutes and both knew it; she has a five-month boyfriend whose virtues she inventoried; she has big things to work through.
- **THE BLURT: "I don't."** Out before it cleared any committee. He smiles — good smile, reaches his eyes — says **"Okay,"** drinks his coffee, and looks at the road.
- **Ami's three hypotheses (she waits three full seconds, then revises):**
  1. *Gracious, declining to press an advantage* — **rejected**: he's watching the road, and a man declining an advantage watches for the effect of the decline.
  2. *Genuinely dense specimen* — signal arrives in plain Japanese from ten inches and fails to decode.
  3. **CORRECT: he decoded it perfectly and could not make it mean what it means, because the model he's running contains no term for a woman wanting him. So the data got thrown out as noise. Again.** She knows it's right "the way she knew a proof was finished, all at once and without triumph."
- **She accepts the cost** — repetition, unambiguity, humiliating directness — and registers that **she is standing in a line with at least two other women in it and one of them famous.** Her response is to sit down and **lay out a schedule.**
- **Close:** *"Tell me about the shrine. All eighteen items. Start at the top."* / "You don't want to hear about a shrine roof at half twelve at night." / *"I took a rooftop unit apart in thirty-four-degree heat for the entertainment value."* She sits knees a hand's width from his, pushes the egg sandwich to his side because he's already eaten both pieces of chicken. **Byl starts at the top.** Lucy lies across both their feet, tail going thump-thump-thump on wet asphalt, **one hour eleven minutes, and Ami never once looks at the time.**

## STATE DELTAS

- **Minako:** knows she was fourteen and begging someone not to leave; knows the figure was surgically removed and the background repainted; has the name **Lucille** with no source. Has **not** connected Byl to the gap — but she has connected *Lucy* to *Lucille* at the level of the body, and she is the one Senshi trained to look for what isn't there. **Has not broken up with Ryō. Has not told him anything.** Owes Byl an answer to his question.
- **Ami:** **has his name.** Attraction fully acknowledged and, uniquely among the five, *experimentally validated* — she ran the confound and it didn't hold. Has diagnosed his core wound correctly on one night's data. Has a standing conversational in with the shrine job. **No Silver Millennium memory has surfaced for her yet** — she's the only one of the three recent POVs with no crack in the redaction.
- **Byl:** now aware, in his own words, that a woman flirted with him on a roof and that he does not understand any of it. Told Ami "nobody wants anything off me" as a description of the weather. **Still has not connected anything.** Five and a half years of evidence he's read exactly backwards. His dream has still not advanced.
- **The redaction, three data points now:** Rei (deliberate search, clean-edged holes, Ch. 10) → Minako (ambush via her own voice, a *finished* hole, Ch. 12) → and the two independently converge on **the fourth column of the east colonnade**: Rei saw the tally scratched at 15, Minako is caught mid-errand at 14 with the pin in her fist. Neither knows the other has anything.
- **Lucy as the trigger mechanism:** she whined the two notes right before Minako's memory and has now physically inserted herself between Byl and three different women (Rei's goma threshold, the parapet, the gas station chairs). Still no gray on the muzzle.
- **The line, as of Ch. 13:** Rei (attraction live, believes him dead, six weeks of daily access) · Minako (flirting, boyfriend, unresolved, has his number) · Ami (attraction validated, has his name, has a schedule) · Michiru (still collecting the third meeting) · Makoto (diner, unfired) · Hotaru (numbers traded, unfired).
- **Ryō:** intact, decent, uninformed, and asleep.

